1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,187
The Art of Deep Reading.

2
00:00:02,137 --> 00:00:07,300
Deep reading differs qualitatively from the rapid scanning typical of online reading.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:11,587
It demands sustained, undistracted engagement with a text.

4
00:00:11,587 --> 00:00:19,362
During deep reading, the brain constructs a mental model of the content, connecting it to prior knowledge and personal experience.

5
00:00:19,362 --> 00:00:24,112
This process builds critical thinking, empathy, and sustained attention.

6
00:00:24,112 --> 00:00:31,662
Research by Maryanne Wolf indicates that screen reading encourages skimming, whereas paper reading promotes deeper comprehension.

7
00:00:31,662 --> 00:00:39,812
Cultivating deep reading requires 30 uninterrupted minutes, with the phone in another room and material that slightly challenges the reader.

8
00:00:39,812 --> 00:00:44,700
Reading at a pace that allows inner voicing of the text enhances comprehension.

9
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:51,125
This practice is increasingly countercultural and, for that very reason, increasingly valuable.

